fas fa-spinner fa-spin small"></i> </em> views </span> <span class="readtime" data-bs-toggle="tooltip" data-bs-placement="bottom" title="1571 words" > <em>8 min</em> read</span></div></div></div></header><div id="toc-bar" class="d-flex align-items-center justify-content-between invisible"> <span class="label text-truncate">NDIAS Auto/IoT CTF: Tiny Crackme Writeup</span> <button type="button" class="toc-trigger btn me-1"> <i class="fa-solid fa-list-ul fa-fw"></i> </button></div><button id="toc-solo-trigger" type="button" class="toc-trigger btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm"> <span class="label ps-2 pe-1">Contents</span> <i class="fa-solid fa-angle-right fa-fw"></i> </button> <dialog id="toc-popup" class="p-0"><div class="header d-flex flex-row align-items-center justify-content-between"><div class="label text-truncate py-2 ms-4">NDIAS Auto/IoT CTF: Tiny Crackme Writeup</div><button id="toc-popup-close" type="button" class="btn-close btn-sm mx-3" aria-label="Close"></button></div><div id="toc-popup-content" class="px-4 py-3 pb-4"></div></dialog><div class="content"><p>After the CTF ended I decided to see if I can solve the Reverse Engineering challenge. It was labelled, and I thought how hard could it be really. I was in for a surprise! This is my first writeup for a RE challenge, so I might be over simplifying or over complicating certain stuff. But since I am a beginner in RE, expect this writeup to be more catered towards beginners like me.</p><h2 id="first-look"><span class="me-2">First Look</span><a href="#first-look" class="anchor text-muted"><i class="fas fa-hashtag"></i></a></h2><p>We are given a binary and a run script. Just by looking at the run script we can see that it is an ARM binary:</p><div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="code-header"> <span data-label-text="Plaintext"><i class="fas fa-code fa-fw small"></i></span> <button aria-label="copy" data-title-succeed="Copied!"><i class="far fa-clipboard"></i></button></div><div class="highlight"><code><table class="rouge-table"><tbody><tr><td class="rouge-gutter gl"><pre class="lineno">1
2
3
4
5
6
7
8
